---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../shared/components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { MAIN_SITE_URL } from "../../../../shared/config/config";

const siteTitle = "Porn Recovery Knowledge Platform";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  name: "Relapse After 90 Days",
  url: MAIN_SITE_URL + "/relapse/after-90-days/",
  description: "What community members report about relapsing after roughly 90 days without pornography use.",
  author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "SelfControlAtlas Tech Team" },
  isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", "name": "Porn Recovery Knowledge Platform", "url": "https://selfcontrolatlas.com" },
};

---
<BaseLayout
  siteTitle={siteTitle}
  siteUrl={MAIN_SITE_URL}
  title="Relapse After 90 Days — Porn Recovery Knowledge Platform"
  description="What community members report about relapsing after roughly 90 days without pornography use."
  canonical="/relapse/after-90-days/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", url: "/" },
    { name: "About Relapse", url: "/relapse/" },
    { name: "After 90 days", url: "/relapse/after-90-days/" },
  ]}
>
  <h1>Relapse After 90 Days</h1>
  <p>Some community members describe a relapse after roughly 90 days of not using
  pornography. Because 90 days is a well-known community goal, a relapse at this point can
  feel especially discouraging.</p>

  <h2>What members report</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A relapse after a long streak is often described as following a reappearing trigger
    or a stressful event, sometimes combined with a moment of overconfidence.</li>
    <li>Members sometimes describe a relapse after 90 days as feeling like "losing
    everything," even though the previous 90 days still happened.</li>
    <li>Several describe a single slip turning into a short binge, then a restart.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What this means</h2>
  <p>The 90-day mark is a community goal with no demonstrated scientific significance, and
  a relapse at this point is not a special kind of failure. The period of control that came
  before is not erased by a single event.</p>

  <p class="note">See <a href="/relapse/recovery-after-relapse/">recovering after a
  relapse</a>, <a href="/patterns/post-relapse-binge/">the post-relapse binge pattern</a>,
  and <a href="/problems/what-is-the-90-day-challenge/">what the 90-day challenge actually
  is</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
